WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.133
-We're hanging out
with an incredible actor.

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.234
Jonah Hill right here. I --

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:06.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:08.100
The new movie is called
"Don't Look Up."

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.133
It's in theaters on Friday.

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:12.400
And on -- on Netflix
December 24th.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.067
Can you talk about
what this movie is about?

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:16.434
It's very funny, by the way,
but it's -- it's --

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:18.767
It's very, like, smart funny,
I think, to me, like --

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:21.534
-Yeah. It's -- It --
So, Adam McKay made this movie,

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:23.234
and Leonardo DiCaprio
and Jennifer Lawrence

00:00:23.234 --> 00:00:26.934
play scientists who see a comet
coming to destroy Earth.

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:30.234
And the world's gonna end
in like six months.

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:32.267
So they take it all the way up
to the president,

00:00:32.267 --> 00:00:34.000
who is played by Meryl Streep,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.801
and I'm her son
and chief of staff, Jason.

00:00:38.801 --> 00:00:44.300
And -- And we deny
the comet's existence.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.434
So, Adam is a brilliant guy.

00:00:46.434 --> 00:00:49.200
And he's kind of
very satirically

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.701
dealing with some of these
issues that have been massive,

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:55.033
where it's kind of
denial of science, let's say.

00:00:55.033 --> 00:01:00.100
Um, and so I play, like,
this kind of spoiled rich kid

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:04.367
who is the son of the president
who is a chief of staff.

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:05.934
And one of the things
I found fun --

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:07.701
You wanna show the picture?
-I do wanna show the picture

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:09.601
'cause I wanna show
your character.

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:13.634
Here's your character right here
holding a purse.

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:17.000
-Yeah, he's a little bitchy
prince. That's how I would --

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.801
-That's your mother.
-Meryl Streep.

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:21.501
And those are the nerd,
like, astronomers behind us.

00:01:21.501 --> 00:01:24.267
That's what Jason would say,
not me.

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:27.667
But -- So one of the things was
they're like, "Okay, well..."

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:32.701
Let's just say there was
a dynamic, at the time,

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:36.567
where there was a high-up
political figure who perhaps

00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:40.133
inappropriately sexualized
his daughter.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:43.567
I'm not gonna name names.
-Okay. Yeah.

00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:47.567
-So my thought was,
"Well, oh, I'm the son.

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:50.467
And most rich kids
look up to their father.

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:53.100
I'm gonna be someone who
worships, like, the mother."

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.234
So I thought it'd be interesting
to play on that

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:59.067
as to inappropriately sexualize
my mother in the role.

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:03.267
And then also
since he admires the feminine,

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:06.267
my first thought was he's gotta
have a Birkin bag.

00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:08.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:10.000
And the other thing was

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.334
I wanted to make if
Fyre Festival was a person.

00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:16.934
That was sort of my ideology
of it, yeah.

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:19.200
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.701
If Fyre Festival was a person.
-Yeah.

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:23.734
-That's who you're playing
in "Don't Look Up."

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:26.701
But how cool was it to act
opposite Meryl Streep?

00:02:26.701 --> 00:02:28.234
-It's so cool.
And she's so cool.

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:30.334
And everyone goes on talk shows
and you're like,

00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:32.200
"This person's cool.
That person's cool."

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.801
Meryl Streep's actually cool.

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:35.968
And she's the best actor.

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:39.667
In fact, I've been -- So, we've
been doing press for this movie,

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:43.033
and in the interviews the past
couple days, I keep saying,

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:45.234
"Oh, and, you know, getting to
work with Meryl, she's the GOAT.

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:46.734
She's the GOAT, right?"

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:49.601
Which, if you know, stands for
Greatest Of All Time, right?

00:02:49.601 --> 00:02:51.467
That's, like, an acronym
that you use for, like,

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:54.067
Michael Jordan
or Jay-Z or whoever,

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:56.634
or, you know, whoever your GOAT
is for whatever you're into.

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:58.234
-Yeah.
-And Meryl to me is the GOAT.

00:02:58.234 --> 00:03:00.701
She's the greatest of all time.
So the whole week, I'm saying,

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:02.434
"You know,
working with Meryl is the best.

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:04.033
She's the GOAT.
She's the GOAT."

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:06.968
And then today, we're doing a
press conference and she's like,

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:09.868
"You know, and Jonah
is so comfortable with me,

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:12.667
he's been calling me
a goat all week."

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:15.868
And -- And she's like --

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:17.501
And I'm like,
"What the [bleep]?"

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:20.467
And I'm like -- I'm like --

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:22.100
And Jennifer Lawrence
explained to her.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.901
'Cause she was telling Jennifer
about this.

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:27.334
How she -- And she's so cool,
she wasn't even offended by it.

00:03:27.334 --> 00:03:29.200
She was just like,
"I guess he, like, loves me

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.334
and is calling me a goat."

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:32.167
And -- And Jennifer's like,
"No, Meryl.

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:33.901
It stands for
Greatest Of All Time."

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:37.501
So she was like, "Hey, thanks
for calling me the GOAT.

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:39.734
I thought you were calling me
a goat this whole time."

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:41.701
And I was like,
"Meryl, you're, like,

00:03:41.701 --> 00:03:44.033
the greatest of all time."
-And she's still cool about it.

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:45.534
Yeah, she really is.
Meryl Streep.

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:47.534
-Shout-out to the GOAT!
Meryl Streep.

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:50.834
Yeah.
-The greatest of all time.

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:52.634
It's very good.
It's very well-written,

00:03:52.634 --> 00:03:54.234
very well-acted,
very well-directed.

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:55.634
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:57.434
Here's our pal Jonah Hill
in "Don't Look Up."

00:03:57.434 --> 00:03:59.000
Take a look at this.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.400
-Dr. Randall, you are now

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.200
the chief science adviser
to the White House.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.601
-What?
-And as such,

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:06.334
we need you to attend
an emergency cabinet meeting

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:07.934
where you will be
fully debriefed.

00:04:07.934 --> 00:04:09.634
-What about us?

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:11.234
-You do not have clearance
for this, sweetheart.

00:04:11.234 --> 00:04:14.767
Don't trip. Got you
some crackers, some waters.

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:16.567
-You don't need to throw it
on the floor.

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:18.300
-It's going to be three,
four hours, tops.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:21.567
-Here, Kate. I don't know
why he's doing that.

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:23.868
-What if we have to go
to the bathroom?

00:04:23.868 --> 00:04:25.868
-We'll lay out some newspaper
for you,

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:27.501
grab you a can of Febreze.

00:04:27.501 --> 00:04:29.501
-Hey. Short, sweet,
and simple science.

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:30.634
-I'll be back.

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:34.601
-Science tells the truth,
Randall.

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:38.400
-You want to come?
-Yeah.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.801 --> 00:04:40.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:40.934 --> 00:04:43.734
-What a jerk!
-Yo, real quick.

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:47.000
Before we end,
I'm not a political man.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.834
But I do believe
in climate change,

00:04:48.834 --> 00:04:51.200
and my girlfriend will kill me
if I don't read this.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.734
I just will say I don't know
how to deal with this stuff.

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:55.367
It feels like Mt. Everest.

00:04:55.367 --> 00:04:57.300
You can call or e-mail
your congressperson

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.367
and ask them to support
H.R. 794,

00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:01.834
the National Climate
Change Emergency.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:05.167
That's it. Very easy.
If you're into it.

00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:06.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.467
-You're welcome any time, buddy.
I love you.

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:10.300
-Thank you, bro. Thank you.
-Jonah Hill, everybody.

